# Part 4: Security Architecture

## Authentication Flow

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ USER OPENS APP                                                   │
└─────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┘
                      │
           ┌──────────▼───────────┐
           │ Check localStorage   │
           │ for accessToken      │
           └─────────┬────────────┘
                     │
        ┌────────────┴────────────┐
        │                         │
   ┌────▼────┐              ┌────▼────┐
   │ Token    │              │ No      │
   │ found &  │              │ token   │
   │ valid?   │              │         │
   └────┬─────┘              └────┬────┘
        │ YES                     │ NO
        │                  ┌──────▼──────┐
        │                  │ Show login  │
        │                  │ page        │
        │                  └──────┬──────┘
        │                         │
        │         ┌───────────────▼──────────────┐
        │         │ User enters credentials     │
        │         │ POST /api/auth/login        │
        │         └───────────────┬──────────────┘
        │                         │
        │         ┌───────────────▼──────────────┐
        │         │ Backend validates           │
        │         │ - Check email in auth_users │
        │         │ - Compare password (bcrypt) │
        │         │ - Create Firebase custom    │
        │         │   token with claims        │
        │         │ - Return accessToken +      │
        │         │   refreshToken             │
        │         └───────────────┬──────────────┘
        │                         │
        │         ┌───────────────▼──────────────┐
        │         │ Frontend stores tokens      │
        │         │ accessToken: localStorage  │
        │         │ refreshToken: httpOnly     │
        │         └───────────────┬──────────────┘
        │                         │
        └────────────────┬────────┘
                         │
             ┌───────────▼──────────┐
             │ Send auth header to  │
             │ all API requests:    │
             │                      │
             │ Authorization:       │
             │ Bearer accessToken   │
             └───────────┬──────────┘
                         │
         ┌───────────────▼───────────────┐
         │ Backend middleware verifies:  │
         │ 1. JWT signature              │
         │ 2. Token not expired          │
         │ 3. User claims (role, bizId)  │
         │ 4. Request matches claims     │
         │                               │
         │ If invalid → Return 401       │
         │ If valid → Process request    │
         └───────────────┬───────────────┘
                         │
                    ┌────▼─────┐
                    │ Response  │
                    │ returned  │
                    └───────────┘
```

## Token Structure (JWT)

```
Header:
{
  "alg": "HS256",
  "typ": "JWT"
}

Payload:
{
  "uid": "firebase_uid_123",
  "email": "owner@kitchen.com",
  "role": "owner",  // owner | manager | driver | admin
  "businessId": "biz_xyz",
  "staffId": "staff_abc",  // Only for drivers
  "branchId": "branch_1",  // Only for managers & drivers
  "iat": 1700000000,       // Issued at
  "exp": 1700000900        // Expires in 15 min (owners) or 24 hrs (drivers)
}

Signature:
HMACSHA256(
  base64UrlEncode(header) + "." +
  base64UrlEncode(payload),
  your-secret-key
)
```

## Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

| Resource | Owner | Manager | Driver | Admin |
|----------|-------|---------|--------|-------|
| /owner/* | ✅ Own only | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ All |
| /manager/* | ✅ Own | ✅ Own branch only | ❌ | ✅ All |
| /driver/* | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ Own only | ✅ All |
| /admin/* | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ Only |

## Data Isolation (Multi-Tenant)

Every API endpoint enforces:

```typescript
// Pseudocode in middleware
function enforceDataIsolation(request) {
  const { role, businessId, staffId } = request.auth.claims;
  
  // Owner: can only access their own business
  if (role === 'owner') {
    if (request.businessId !== businessId) {
      return FORBIDDEN;
    }
  }
  
  // Manager: can only access their branch
  if (role === 'manager') {
    if (request.businessId !== businessId || 
        request.branchId !== managerBranchId) {
      return FORBIDDEN;
    }
  }
  
  // Driver: can only access their own deliveries
  if (role === 'driver') {
    if (request.businessId !== businessId || 
        request.staffId !== staffId) {
      return FORBIDDEN;
    }
  }
  
  // Admin: full access
  if (role !== 'admin') {
    // Continue with request
  }
}
```

## Password Security

```
Owner/Manager Registration:
  1. User enters password in signup form
  2. Frontend hashes with PBKDF2 (optional, for extra layer)
  3. Send to /api/auth/signup over HTTPS
  4. Backend hashes with bcrypt (cost = 12)
  5. Store only hash in Firestore (/auth_users/{uid}/password_hash)
  6. Never log or return password

Driver PIN Security:
  1. Owner enters PIN in Settings (e.g., 1234)
  2. Frontend sends plaintext to /api/owner/staff
  3. Backend hashes with bcrypt (cost = 10, faster for PINs)
  4. Store only hash in Firestore:
     - /driver_auth/{phone}
     - /businesses/{bizId}/staff/{staffId}
  5. Driver enters PIN on login
  6. Backend compares: bcrypt.compare(inputPin, storedHash)
  7. Rate limit: 5 failures → 15 min lockout
```

## Firestore Security Rules (Deny All Client Access)

```
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    // DENY EVERYTHING
    // Only Vercel backend (via Firebase Admin SDK) can read/write
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
```

All database access goes through the Vercel API layer, which uses Firebase Admin SDK.

