# Part 8: Security Checklist

- [ ] All passwords hashed with bcrypt (cost ≥ 10)
- [ ] All API endpoints require JWT token
- [ ] JWT tokens expire (15 min for owners, 24 hrs for drivers)
- [ ] Refresh tokens stored in HttpOnly cookies
- [ ] All requests logged with IP, user, action, timestamp
- [ ] Rate limiting on auth endpoints (5 failures → 15 min lockout)
- [ ] SQL injection prevention (using parameterized queries)
- [ ] CSRF tokens on forms
- [ ] CORS configured to only allow own domain
- [ ] All external APIs (Razorpay, Gemini) called server-side only
- [ ] Environment variables not hardcoded
- [ ] HTTPS enforced (Vercel + Firebase)
- [ ] Firestore rules deny all client access
- [ ] Service Account Key not exposed in code
- [ ] Sensitive endpoints (admin) have additional verification
- [ ] PII (phone, address) encrypted at rest if required by law
- [ ] Data retention policy documented (delete logs after 90 days)
- [ ] Backup & disaster recovery plan in place

